+# One fresh native home Alpha for registered foreign-refuter findings
+
+This opt-in normal-planner adapter reopens one already completed standalone
+home Alpha unit once. It grants no old acceptance, extra mathematical cycle,
+source permission, native observation, state reset or gate waiver. Existing
+foreign-refuter registration and the separate origin refuter coverage
+continuation remain required. Nothing edits the original native reports.
+
+Root registers `research/RUN-step3-home-alpha-continuations.json`:
+
+```
+{
+  "version": 1,
+  "run": "RUN",
+  "policy": "owner-step3-foreign-refuter-home-alpha-continuation-v1",
+  "authorized_by": "owner",
+  "authorization": "Concrete genuine root authorization, at least 40 characters",
+  "continuations": [ENTRY]
+}
+```
+
+`ENTRY` has:
+
+- `version:1`, exact `run`, `owner_identity:"/root"`, positive string `unit:"30"`,
+  `label:"3a-batch-30-foreign-refuter-continuation-1"`, `canonical_group:"batch-30"`;
+- `mathematical_acceptance:false`, `previous_acceptance_inherited:false`,
+  `historical_artifact_basis:"owner-captured current completed-native artifacts; no structured-output byte attestation"`;
+- concrete `reason` at least80characters and genuine `writers_drained_at` after
+  the successful old native completion and relevant actual writer drain;
+- own-run raw SHA256 `{path,sha256}` references `previous_result`,
+  `previous_attempt`, `previous_prompt`, `previous_report`,
+  `previous_decisions`, `previous_scope`, `registration_manifest`,
+  `owner_capture`, `task`;
+- `current_inputs:[{path,sha256},...]`, exactly the initial actual source/carrier
+  path set described below;
+- `foreign_refuter_routes:[{path,entry_sha256},...]`, exactly every registered
+  foreign-refuter entry targeted at this home unit, without duplicates.
+
+The previous result is the **unchanged actual stable**
+`research/RUN-dispatch/alpha-3a-batch-30.result.json`; previous attempt and prompt
+are its actual `.attempt-N.result.json` and `.attempt-N.prompt.md`. Stable and
+attempt bytes must match; successful native Alpha must cover exactly30, retain
+normal process/terminal completion, prompt binding and timestamps. Legacy
+multi-unit Alpha dispatches are not supported by this narrow route. The old
+native receipt remains old evidence; it never authenticates the new canonical
+report or supplies fresh coverage.
+
+Previous report, decisions and scope MUST be immutable own-run archives, not
+the mutable canonical paths. Root already captured these for this issue in
+`RUN-owner-refuter57-original-evidence/`. Their hashes remain exact after fresh
+native output overwrites the canonical report/decisions. Old native completion
+stdout links both canonical artifacts; it does not contain their full bytes.
+The explicit historical-artifact basis honestly records root's capture instead
+of inventing a structured native-output attestation.
+
+The archived decisions must have `version:1`, exact run, `group:"batch-30"`,
+unique obligations and an array of decisions. Scope must be version2, exact run
+and batch30, assignment `group:"j"` (the current actual assignment, distinct from
+canonical output group). `registration_manifest` archives the actual CURRENT
+`RUN-batch-30.pages.json` after the root mathematical correction/metadata
+integration. Its unique item/page inventory must match archived scope's
+manifest_post/page_manifest_post. Current source mathematics is bound separately
+from historical old review.
+
+`current_inputs` contains exactly, once each:
+
+- `research/RUN-step3-scope-30.json` (same raw hash as previous_scope archive),
+- `research/RUN-batch-30.pages.json` (same raw hash as registration_manifest),
+- `research/RUN-batch-30.proof-contracts.json`,
+- every `items/ID.md` listed in that complete manifest,
+- every `library/CATEGORY/PAGE.md` in that manifest.
+
+All these current guards and both old canonical report/decisions archives are
+checked before the real base Alpha planner can write its order task. A stale
+or exhausted route therefore mutates no task. Doctor checks historical
+authority only; planning unrelated units does not spend this unit's budget.
+
+`owner_capture` is a genuine root capture record:
+
+```
+{version:1,run,unit:"30",owner_identity:"/root",
+ native_acceptance_claimed:false,original_artifact_bytes_native_bound:false,
+ report_sha256:PREVIOUS_REPORT_RAW,
+ decisions_sha256:PREVIOUS_DECISIONS_RAW,
+ scope_sha256:PREVIOUS_SCOPE_RAW,old_result_sha256:PREVIOUS_RESULT_RAW}
+```
+
+It supplements the existing original-evidence receipt without rewriting it.
+This record asserts actual captured bytes, not a new native verdict.
+
+The task must contain canonical group and both exact canonical output paths,
+and every required foreign `gate:DEFECT_ID`. It should explicitly require
+independent redecision of ALL old owed obligations (archived scope/decisions
+and generated ordinary order), both new findings, actual corrected proof,
+full risk review and all normal closed ledger rules. State that prior native
+acceptance/root proof repair supplies no new acceptance and that original
+observed bytes remain unbound where so recorded. Require the normal report and
+canonical decisions group, not the new dispatch-label suffix. The ordinary
+brief has an explicit exact-label rule preserving canonical `G=batch-30`.
+
+For this issue the two existing foreign routes are origin57:index1 and
+origin57:index2, SAME actual lemma/home30, distinct genuine defect IDs:
+
+- `ml101-b57-3a-convex-supporting-line`
+- `ml101-b57-3a-convex-citation`
+
+They remain separately mandatory ordinary gate decisions. Their registry uses
+stable per-entry bindings, so appending them does not change existing47 entry
+or continuation36 bindings. Continuation57's existing refuter wrapper must
+reference BOTH exact entries. No edge57→30 is invented. Preserve original57's
+incorrect home55 prose as native historical evidence, not routing authority.
+
+The stage matcher excludes only old unit30 stable receipts (single and legacy
+duplicate role-prefix aliases) under authenticated registration. It admits
+only exact fresh `alpha-3a-batch-30-foreign-refuter-continuation-1.result.json`;
+attempt files, suffix2, unregistered labels or old stable30 give no coverage.
+Other units and all gates/model/role/brief/covers/timeout/artifacts stay normal.
+Any completed fresh result OR completed attempt, including failure, consumes
+the one shot. A new source/core review cycle or automatic unchanged retry is
+not authorized.
+
+All original owed scope obligations and previous gate decisions are rederived
+for planning, stamp and adjudication/final checks even if a later projection
+omits one. The new native worker must independently write all decisions.
+The full old report/decisions are immutable history, never copied by a tool
+into a fresh verdict. Normal Alpha may independently confirm fatal/nonfatal,
+reject a false positive, amend current source or escalate; all ordinary proof,
+carrier, ledger, risk and native gates apply.
+
+Current report consumers select the registered fresh result identity when
+this route exists. The old stable30 receipt cannot authenticate new report
+bytes. Generic native-created-item eligibility admits the exact registered
+attempt1 only with root/run context; all immutable native provenance checks
+remain. No creation markers are invented for pre-Step3 owner additions.
+
+Closure freezes the full home registry, all old archives/receipt/prompt/task/
+capture refs AND authenticated successful fresh stable receipt, identical
+immutable attempt1 and actual prompt with exact run/role/label/covers/canonical
+assignment. Missing/failed/mismatched fresh completion cannot close. Later
+source amendments do not rewrite the preserved historical source/context.
+
+Apply code only after independent review; root owns registration, genuine
+current guards, source integration/metadata currency, module reload, normal
+planner dispatch, all gates and commits. Never reset state or manually dispatch
+an LLM. If initial home writer is active, drain it before authorization.
+
+Focused durable test:
+`node tools/tsx-run.mjs --test tools/autopilot/test/home-alpha-continuations.test.mts`.
