 # Step 3a adjudication — adjudicator G, run `<run>`
 
+- An owner-registered fresh dispatch `3a-batch-N-foreign-refuter-continuation-1` retains canonical `G=batch-N`, covers exactly batch N, and writes the normal `alpha-batch-N-3a.md` and `alpha-batch-N-3a-decisions.json` with `group: batch-N`. Its fresh result filename is separate. Read the authenticated continuation task and original archived report/decisions/scope; independently re-review every old owed obligation, current risk review and every new required foreign gate. Old acceptance supplies history, never your verdict. For all other labels, follow the ordinary rule below.
 - Set `G` to the suffix of your dispatch label: `3a-batch-13` means `G` is `batch-13`; a retained legacy dispatch `3a-b` means `G` is `b`. Use that suffix in every path and in the decisions file's `group` field below. The scope file's original assignment group stays unchanged.
 - Work only on your `covers:` batches. New dispatches cover exactly one batch. For each batch, read `research/<run>-step3-scope-<i>.json`, its reader report and findings, refuter report, current carriers, and every cited dependency.
 - Follow `research/<run>-alpha-G-3a-order.task.md` within your dispatched batches. Adjudicate routed items from lowest to highest in-run dependency level, complete each item's risk review before moving higher, and keep all findings for one item together. Page-only obligations retain their own scope. Escalate affected consumers outside your dispatched batches to the owner for supplier-first repair rather than editing another adjudicator's files.
